=begin rakudoc
=TITLE The Raku documentation suite built using Elucid8

=head General deployment

Obtain an container image by running I<Podman> | I<Docker> using C<New_Website/Dockerfile>.
=item During the image generation, the document sources are pulled into the workspace from their
repos;
=item the HTML files and other assets are generated
=item the HTML & assets are packaged with Caddy
=item a CMD is set so that caddy serves the HTML in answer to HTTP messages on :80

=head Local deployment

Local deployment is intended for those who wish to contribute to this repository by modifying
the index files in C<site-sources> or the plugins in C<local-lib>.

=item Clone the repo with C<git clone https://github.com/raku/doc-website.git raku-doc-website>
=item Modify files in repo as need be
=item create image (see below)
=item run a container using image (see below)
=item inspect generated website by pointing browser at C<localhost:3000>

For local deployment, it is better to use a Cro app rather than Caddy.

head2 Create image & run a container
=item assuming the current working directory in your local terminal is raku-doc-wehsite as cloned using git
=begin numitem
Create an image called RakuDocumentation by running I<Podman> using C<New_Website/LocalContainer.dockerfile>.
=for code :lang<text>
cd New_Website
podman build -f=LocalContainer.dockerfile -t=RakuDocumentation .
=end numitem

=head2 Running the image as a container

Assuming the image is RakuDocumentation
=code podman run --rm -d --name=rdw  --network=host RakuDocumentation

Point the browser to C<localhost:3000>, which means that in the browser's URL window, type C<localhost:3000>.

Once inspecting is complete, the container will need to be removed, eg.
=code podman stop rdw
=end rakudoc